          "page": 4,
          "section": "results and discussion",
          "quote": "Second, more TBs are found in the gradient layer at 10 % under 88 K, and denser dislocations accompanied with twins featuring a smaller average spacing (6.2 nm versus 17.9 nm for undeformed state) and higher volume fraction (57.1% versus 46.4%), compared with the undeformed state, are observed in Supplementary Figs. S4 and S7.",
